{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Until</b> — a poetic figure: עַד עֵת בֹּא דְבָרוֹ. The meaning: that the word of the dream came when he interpreted it, like כִּי יָבֹא דְבָרְךָ (Genesis 41:32)." "<b>The word of YHWH refined him</b> — that HaShem placed in his mouth the true interpretation; therefore his interpretation went forth refined without dross. And note the he and the vav in the word צְרָפְתְּהוּ, which refers back to the matter of Joseph. And there are those who say: when the matter of Joseph came before HaShem, then His word refined him — that is the decree that He decreed."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 105, :notes {1 "The phrase הנה הה\"א והוי\"ו במלת צרפתהו שבה אל דבר יוסף is read hyper-literally; שבה אל may mean 'refers back to,' but the syntax is compressed and somewhat obscure."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:29.905738015Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}